# Line-ending policy for the whole repository.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` tells Git: treat every file as text by default,
# store LF in the repository, and check out LF on every OS (no CRLF
# conversion). This keeps line endings identical across Windows/Linux/macOS
# contributors, so `git status` no longer lights up whole files just because
# an editor or `core.autocrlf` flipped CR/LF.
#
# See the CRLF explainer in the commit that added this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files — Git must never touch their bytes (no line-ending / diff).
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.bmp  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tar  binary
*.bin  binary
*.hex  binary
*.elf  binary
*.uf2  binary
*.db   binary
*.dtb  binary
*.lib  binary
*.a    binary
